# SUPPLIED stimulus for whole minion_tlb (B11), derived from the PINNED
# CORE-ET DV sequence, not invented here.
#
# SOURCE.  hw/ip/minion/tlb/dv/minion_tlb_test.cc:299, the FIRST existing
# fill_entry call: fill_entry(sim, 0, vpn_for_idx(1, 0x11), 0xABCDE, ...).
# Packed against the pinned minion_pkg.sv / tlb_pkg.sv structs for THIS
# artifact's configuration (NrMinions = 1, Entries = 8), so the wrapper's
# two-minion vectors are NOT copied:
#
#   req_data_i      (ordinal  7, w48) = 0x580000001110   vpn 0x111 at 39:4
#   satp_info_i     (ordinal 11, w32) = 0x80010000       mode 8, ppn 0x10000
#   ptw_resp_data_i (ordinal  5, w64) = 0x2af378c7       ppn 0xABCDE at 53:10
#
# Expected committed word at address 1: 0x223600abcde = {req_tag_q, entry},
# tag 0x22 recomputed as vpn >> 3 for the one-minion index width.
#
# THE WRITE CONDITION is registered.  minion_tlb.sv:332 is
#   rf_latch_wr_en = !ptw_req_invalidated && ptw_resp_valid_q && !canceled_req
# -- `ptw_resp_valid_q`, not `_i`.  The pinned test holds the PTW response for
# TWO ticks for exactly this reason, and under P=2 each source tick is two
# sub-steps, so the hold is widened accordingly below.
#
# Constants: ready high, no invalidate, no coop mode, base page size.
in 4 1 1          # ptw_req_ready_i
in 12 1 0         # tlb_invalidate_i
in 1 1 0          # coop_mode_i
in 13 2 0         # vmspagesize_i
in 8 1 0          # req_min_id_i
in 3 32 0         # matp_info_i
in 11 32 2147549184        # satp_info_i = 0x80010000
in 7 48 96757023511824     # req_data_i  = 0x580000001110
in 5 64 716267719          # ptw_resp_data_i = 0x2af378c7
#
# RESET: rst_ni LOW for the first two sub-steps, then HIGH.
at 0 in 10 1 0
at 1 in 10 1 0
in 10 1 1
#
# REQUEST: req_valid_i high while the request is presented.
at 0 in 9 1 0
at 1 in 9 1 0
at 2 in 9 1 1
at 3 in 9 1 1
#
# PTW RESPONSE, held across four sub-steps = two source ticks, so the
# registered `ptw_resp_valid_q` the write condition reads is asserted.
at 0 in 6 1 0
at 1 in 6 1 0
at 2 in 6 1 0
at 3 in 6 1 0
at 4 in 6 1 1
at 5 in 6 1 1
at 6 in 6 1 1
at 7 in 6 1 1
